# FIX131 — the live backend no longer bind-mounts this directory, so what the
# image contains is what runs. Keep runtime data and local caches out of it:
# uploads/ holds users' avatars (it is a named volume at runtime, see
# docker-compose.yml) and must never be copied into an image layer by a
# `docker compose build` run from a working checkout. (scripts/build-images.sh
# builds from `git archive`, which already leaves gitignored files out.)
# The same context also builds ner-service (ner_service/Dockerfile copies only
# ner_service/), which none of this touches.
uploads/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
